格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: GitHub repository & issue search, repo/issue details, and file reading tools (github_search / github_get) · DeepSeek Harness 插件:GitHub 仓库与 issue 检索、详情与文件读取,匿名可用,可选只读 token 解锁代码搜索","id":"gh:1335286837","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-github","slug":"moxingovo/dsh-github","topics":["agent-tool","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","github","github-api","search"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: GitHub repository & issue search, repo/issue details, and file reading tool"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"s (github_search / github_get) · DeepSeek Harness 插件:GitHub 仓库与 issue 检索、详情与文件读取,匿名可用,可选只读 token 解锁代"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"github_search / github_get) · DeepSeek Harness 插件:GitHub 仓库与 issue 检索、详情与文件读取,匿名可用,可选只读 token 解锁代码搜索"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-github"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文 | **English** · Changelog · Releases"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A **GitHub retrieval plugin** for DeepSeek Harness.\nAfter install the agent gains two tools:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- `github_search` — find repositories and issues/PRs with native GitHub search syntax\n(e.g. `repo:ve"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"rcel/next.js is:issue`, `agent harness language:typescript`).\n- `github_get` — read one resource in "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"full: repository metadata, an issue or pull-request body, or a\ndecoded file (optionally at a specifi"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"metadata, an issue or pull-request body, or a\ndecoded file (optionally at a specific branch or tag)."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Anonymous by default (60 requests per hour per IP). Set a read-only fine-grained token to unlock cod"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"e\nsearch and raise the limit to 5000 per hour. Read-only by design: the plugin never creates issues,"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"the limit to 5000 per hour. Read-only by design: the plugin never creates issues,\ncomments, or code."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> Unofficial community plugin — not affiliated with DeepSeek or GitHub.\n>\n> **Harness compatibility*"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"*: **0.1.4** is verified on **DeepSeek Harness 0.1.7-rc.2**, and 0.1.3 on\n> **0.1.6-alpha.2** — **no"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" runtime code change was needed for either**. The 0.1.0–0.1.7 lines all work.\n> Version map in Compa"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"code change was needed for either**. The 0.1.0–0.1.7 lines all work.\n> Version map in Compatibility."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Restart `dsh web`. New conversations gain `github_search` and `github_get`."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Mount it in an agent preset instead when only that preset should see the tools:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Optional token"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Create a fine-grained personal access token with **Repository access = Public Repositories\n(read-onl"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"y)**, then put it in the environment or in your `$DSH_HOME/.env` (the launcher injects every\n`KEY=VA"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"LUE` line of that file into the server process):"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Without a token everything still works anonymously; only code search and the higher rate limit need "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"it.\nThe token is never written to configuration files, logs, or tool output."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Key | Default | Meaning |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| `baseUrl` | `https://api.github.com` | API host (must be an http/https URL). |\n| `token` | — | Lit"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"eral token (secret; prefer `tokenEnv`). |\n| `tokenEnv` | `GITHUB_TOKEN` | Environment variable namin"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"g the optional token. |\n| `userAgent` | `dsh-github` | User-Agent header. |\n| `requestTimeoutMs` | `"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"30000` | Per-request timeout (ms). |\n| `searchMaxPerPage` | `30` | Page-size ceiling for `github_sea"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"rch` (API maximum 100). |\n| `fileMaxChars` | `200000` | File character cap for `github_get` (value-l"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"evel, with a `truncated` flag). |\n| `timeoutMs` | `30000` | Cooperative tool-call timeout budget. |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Override any field in `profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` — later layers win per row:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"This package is self-contained: it registers the tools and carries its own GitHub REST provider\n(`gi"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"thub-api`). It does **not** publish a `ctx.github` service, so no other plugin can consume it by\nser"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"vice key (an earlier in-tree line did — see Compatibility)."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Tools and error codes"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"`github_search` takes `query` (required), `kind` (`repositories` default, or `issues` — which includ"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"es\npull requests), `page`, and `perPage` (≤ 30). `github_get` takes `kind` (`repo` | `issue` | `file"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"`),\n`owner`, `repo`, plus `number` for issues and `path` (with optional `ref`) for files. File paths"},{"id":"p24s4","text":" are\npercent-encoded segment by segment, so spaces, non-ASCII names and `#`/`?` work; with `ref` the"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" returned\n`htmlUrl` points at that revision rather than HEAD."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Tools fail with structured errors carrying these codes:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Code | Meaning |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| `GITHUB_UNAUTHORIZED` | 401 — needs a token (typically code search). |\n| `GITHUB_FORBIDDEN` | 403 "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"— rate limit or insufficient permissions. |\n| `GITHUB_NOT_FOUND` | 404 — repository, issue or path d"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"oes not exist. |\n| `GITHUB_API_ERROR` | 422 invalid search syntax, or another non-2xx status. |\n| `G"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ITHUB_BAD_RESPONSE` | Non-JSON response body. |\n| `GITHUB_REDIRECT_REFUSED` | A redirect was refused"},{"id":"p27s5","text":" — the credential-safety guard. |\n| `GITHUB_TLS_UNTRUSTED` | The HTTPS connection was re-signed by a"},{"id":"p27s6","text":" proxy, antivirus scanner, or a local accelerator, and this runtime trusts only its built-in CA list"},{"id":"p27s7","text":" — see the TLS caveat under Skills. |\n| `GITHUB_REQUEST_FAILED` | Network failure, including timeout"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"s; since 0.1.6 the message carries the underlying code (e.g. `[ECONNREFUSED]`). |\n| `GITHUB_FILE_TOO"},{"id":"p27s9","text":"_LARGE` | The API does not inline files over 1MB, so no content is returned. |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Two independent boundaries apply to file reads: the API inlines at most 1MB (`GITHUB_FILE_TOO_LARGE`"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"\nabove), and the tool truncates at `fileMaxChars` (default 200000) with `truncated: true`."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Skills"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Two companion skills ship in `skills/`:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- `plugin-tool-github` — tool usage: arguments, search syntax, error routing, fallbacks.\n- `plugin-w"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"eb-github` — the host-side provider: config keys, the `GITHUB_TOKEN` credential, rate\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- The token is read from the environment (or an explicit literal config value) only; it never enters"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"\nlogs or tool output.\n- Every request refuses redirects, so the token can never be forwarded to anot"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"her origin.\n- The token is sent only to the configured API host (`api.github.com` by default).\n- No "},{"id":"p33s4","text":"write operations of any kind: the plugin cannot create issues, comment, or push code."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Plugin | DeepSeek Harness | Notes |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"| 0.1.4 | **0.1.7-rc.2** | Verified; runtime unchanged. `devDependencies` now target `@deepseek-ai/*"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"@0.1.7-rc.2`, so the typecheck is the compatibility check. |\n| 0.1.3 | 0.1.6-alpha.2 | Verified; run"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"time unchanged (the plugin uses no typert codec API). |\n| 0.1.2 | 0.1.0 – 0.1.6 | Path encoding + re"},{"id":"p36s4","text":"f-aware `htmlUrl`. |\n| 0.1.0–0.1.1 | 0.1.0 line | `github_search` / `github_get`. |"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Live-verified on 0.1.7-rc.2: `github_search` (repositories and issues) and `github_get`\n(`repo` and "},{"id":"p37s2","text":"`file`). Typecheck, build and all 7 tests pass against `@deepseek-ai/*@0.1.7-rc.2`."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
